  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ICT Coordinator Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Human rights abuses and environmental problems in the electronics sector are endemic and need to be addressed with a more integrated approach that will breach the gap between social and environmental approaches as well as making links between consumers and electronics workers from different continents. In 2006 a group of environmental, human rights and development NGOs, union representatives and grassroots organisations agreed to set up a coordination point with a dedicated electronics campaigns coordinator to improve information sharing and facilitate a network working to improve standards in the electronics industry (ICT, mobile phones, televisions.) Organisations in the network will support workers through dialogue with electronics companies, organising and community based activities, sharing of research and information, lobbying for regulation, campaigning, and other efforts, aimed at improving labour, environmental conditions and human rights in the sector.

The aim of the coordinating structure is that it will be a light and flexible tool to increase the impact of national and international campaigns and support organising and networking at grassroots level. SOMO which is hosting the coordination point will provide line management of the coordinator post on a day to day basis. The Advisory Committee will ensure that the coordinator&#x2019;s work reflects the right balance of strategic priorities and that the coordinator is linked in to key on-going activities and campaigns globally.</narrative>
  </description>
